div.div:
pincerna , ae, m., =
			πιγκέρνης (v. Du Cange, Gloss.
		Graec. s. h. v.; prop. one who mixes drinks; hence, in gen.), 
I.a cupbearer, butler (post-class.), Ascon. Cic. Verr. 2, 1, 26;
					Lampr. Alex. Sev. 41;
					Hier. Quaest. in Gen. 40, 1;
					Inscr. Orell. 2881; Vulg. Gen.
				40, 1; id. 2 Esdr. 1,
		11.
